otball operations  department inside the nfl she's very  very plugged in  and and helping to run  all of the covid related stuff that is  going on in the league but she's done  more than that  she really has had her hand in almost  every aspect from cap management uh you  know to to covid uh management and  i have been told by a couple of people  in the league that  they will not be surprised to see her  get an interview to either be a gm or  club president in the next year or two  it's long overdue you ask bill parcells  you ask some of the people who have  employed donna ponte  that she definitely can do the job is  totally unintimidated uh by anybody who  just like kim ang  who got the miami marlins gm job many  stories of people in baseball you know  in intimidating ways and she just  wouldn't have it it's the same thing  with donna ponte  one of the fundamental issues in the nfl  when it comes to representation of  minorities and coaching and gm jobs is  that there is gross underrepresentation  of minorities in the ownership ranks  there are plenty of females who are  involved in ownership of nfl teams from  sheila fordham now in detroit from kim  pagula co-owner of the buffalo bills amy  adams strunk controlling owner of the  tennessee titans so  there there are female voices at the  highest levels of the sport  that i think sets the stage uh maybe  even more so than it does for you know  the growth that the nfl has been trying  to get in minority representation the  female representation becomes easier  peter when you have so many female  owners and it seems like there are more  all the time  i think the next step has to be either a  club president or a full-time position  coach exclusive position coach katie  sauer has done a great job in san  francisco i'd like to see katie sauers  being handed a high level position job  you know or cali bronson at some point  soon that to me is the next step and  getting donna ponte a high level job  with one of the teams 